GSoC'2014 promises to add new features to Tatoeba that will bring it to the
level of Duolingo. So get ready for Lojban courses there.


2014-06-05 14:13 GMT+04:00 Yixuan Zhu <sulzedax@cms.hu-berlin.de>:

> I guess there will still be a lot of tinkering with efficient learning
> methods.
>
> Although I never tried Anki, I have been using Memrise extensively for
> Chinese vocabulary.
> It also has some glitches, too many repetitions for example, but it is
> motivating and
> effective as far as I can tell from around 3 years experience. It counts
> all sessions you do.
>
> There are many well-developed courses on Lojban including interesting
> (even etymological)
> memes (learning aids). So if you want you could try it out. I would
> recommend it to learners
> of any language every day.
>
